  "summary": "Possible typosquat of @solana-labs/anchor (anchor → ancor)",
  "details": "Package name `@solana-labs/ancor` is a single-character deletion from the well-known Solana smart-contract framework `@coral-xyz/anchor` and impersonates the `@solana-labs` scope. Static patterns matched POST/fetch and ping/network primitives in the bundled `lib/index.cjs.js` and `lib/index.esm.js`, but these are keyword co-occurrences in a minified bundle and were not corroborated by traced-code analysis confirming exfiltration intent versus normal RPC client behavior expected of a Solana/Anchor-shaped library. Name-similarity to a top ecosystem package combined with scope impersonation warrants human review of the publisher and bundle contents before allowing.",
